    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d922">

                <pb facs="0832" n="825" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg825"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/11752: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-12-21T12:00:00+09:00">December 21,
                        1937—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received December 21—9:40 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>664. Our 616, December 11, 3 p.m.,<anchor n="43" xml:id="d922-f1"/> march of
                    Japanese troops through the International Settlement at Shanghai.</p>
                <p>The Foreign Office after acknowledging receipt of our note of December 11, 1937,
                    states as follows (translation): <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p rendition="#flush">“With regard thereto, the Foreign Office has the honor
                            to reply that the Japanese Government has, of course, no intention which
                            will impair the administration or the authority of the Municipal
                            Council, and to make the assurance that in the maintenance of peace and
                            order in the International Settlement it is the constant policy of the
                            Japanese Government to cooperate with the International Settlement
                            authorities”.</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>Repeated to Shanghai.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d922-f1" n="43" xml:id="d922-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it reported “Action taken” as instructed in Department’s telegram
                    No. 337, December 10, 6 p.m., <ref target="#pg785">p. 785</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
